---
import CalloutCard from '../cards/CalloutCard.astro';
import PullQuoteCard from '../cards/PullQuoteCard.astro';

/** The About page's editorial body: why it exists, what it publishes, standards, funding. */
interface Props {
	headingId?: string;
}

const { headingId = 'mission' } = Astro.props;

const h3 = 'font-display text-h3 leading-[1.28] font-medium';
const p = 'text-body leading-body mt-5 text-pretty';
---

<section
	aria-labelledby={headingId}
	class='container pt-18'>
	<div class='measure mx-auto'>
		<h2
			id={headingId}
			class='font-display text-h2 tracking-heading leading-[1.2] font-medium'>
			Why this exists
		</h2>

		<p class={p}>
			The Quarry started in 2020 as a set of notes between four editors who had all just been made redundant in the same
			quarter. The notes were about process — how many edits a piece should get, what a correction ought to cost,
			whether anybody was reading past the fold. They were not meant to be published.
		</p>

		<p class={p}>
			Six years later they are the entire publication. We write for the people who run small publications: the founders,
			the editors, the one-person newsletters that pay a mortgage. Everything here is reported from inside that work
			rather than about it from a distance.
		</p>

		<h3 class:list={[h3, 'mt-11']}>What we publish</h3>

		<p class='text-body leading-body mt-4 text-pretty'>
			Four beats, in rough order of volume: essays on independent media, interviews with editors and founders, field
			notes from publications trying something specific, and craft pieces on the mechanics of editing and type.
		</p>

		<ul class='text-body leading-body mt-5 flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6'>
			<li><strong>Essays</strong> — arguments about how the industry works and who it works for.</li>
			<li><strong>Interviews</strong> — long, edited transcripts. The subject sees their quotes before we run.</li>
			<li><strong>Field notes</strong> — short dispatches, usually with numbers attached.</li>
			<li><strong>Craft</strong> — house style, editing passes, typography, the unglamorous half.</li>
		</ul>

		<PullQuoteCard
			quote='If a piece would be better as an email to one person, we send the email instead.'
			caption='House rule, since 2021'
			margin='mt-13'
		/>

		<h3 class:list={[h3, 'mt-13']}>Editorial standards</h3>

		<p class='text-body leading-body mt-4 text-pretty'>
			Every piece gets three passes — structure, argument, line — and no piece ships on its first. Corrections run at
			the top of the affected post, dated, with the original wording intact. We do not take sponsored posts, affiliate
			links, or paid placements in the recommendations list.
		</p>

		<CalloutCard margin='mt-9'>
			Some of the publications we cover have been clients of our writers. Where that is true, it is disclosed in the
			piece.
		</CalloutCard>

		<h3 class:list={[h3, 'mt-13']}>How it's funded</h3>

		<p class='text-body leading-body mt-4 text-pretty'>
			Members, entirely. Free members get the weekly essay and the full archive. Paid members get the interviews, the
			annual field report, and the knowledge that five writers are paid a rate they agreed to rather than accepted.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
